description:
Implement the code half of the canonical four-layer contract agreed on KDATAP-77d2b0: one versioned representation, one structured per-layer eligibility model, one deterministic one-to-one evaluator, and one scorecard vector.

Gold migration is KDATAP-b0d5e2; baseline publication is KDATAP-baca47. Detector retuning and new language ingest remain out of scope.

The representation and graph work are gated by four explicit design rulings:

- per-layer treatment of legacy `subject.name`;
- when component vendor/instance is asserted;
- component entity identity and same-subtype cardinality;
- legacy flow disposition and regold readiness.

Eligibility is additionally gated by the structured outcome ruling, including capacity and processing errors.

Definition of done: every headline metric comes from one evaluator consuming canonical observations from shared adapters; no alternate precision matcher remains; all per-layer eligibility reasons and one-to-one cardinality cases pass synthetic contract tests; no cross-layer scalar is produced.
